---
const story = 'keystone at a glance, in seven steps: 1, you deploy a key set per disk to keystone, a Worker on your Cloudflare account; 2, the computer binds its encrypted disk once to its key set; 3, at boot the computer asks keystone, sending only a blinded value; 4, keystone reads that key set; 5, it answers with the missing half of the key; 6, the computer opens the disk with no passphrase typed, and keystone never sees the disk; 7, if the computer is stolen, you delete its key set before it next starts, keystone refuses it, and the disk stays locked.';
